.TH PRISM-TERM 1 "2026-10-16" "prism-term 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prism-term \- Prism's terminal catalog: animated facets for any terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prism-term
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIid\fR ...]
.br
.B prism-term
.I facet-id
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prism-term
renders Prism's terminal facets (scenes, spinners, progress meters, charts,
text art, TUI controls, diagrams and ops views) with a zero-dependency Node.js
engine. It detects the terminal: color depth (truecolor, 256, 16, mono), glyphs
(braille, sextant and block elements, or 7-bit ASCII) and a light or dark
background (Prism Day or Prism Night).
Without a command it opens the catalog browser on an interactive terminal and
prints the list otherwise.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (none)
The catalog browser: galleries, facets and a live preview.
.TP
.BI play " id ..."
Play facets fullscreen in the live player (several make a playlist; or
\fB\-\-gallery\fR, \fB\-\-category\fR, \fB\-\-kind\fR).
.TP
.B showcase
An auto-advancing tour (\fB\-\-gallery\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR seconds per facet).
.TP
.B list
Facets grouped by gallery and category (\fB\-\-gallery\fR, \fB\-\-category\fR,
\fB\-\-kind\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR, \fB\-\-ids\fR).
.TP
.B galleries
The galleries with their counts and categories.
.TP
.BI info " id"
Size, needs, parameters and the commands for one facet (\fB\-\-json\fR).
.TP
.BI snapshot " id"
A still frame to stdout (ANSI), or to \fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR: \fI.html\fR (\fB\-\-frames\fR
\fIN\fR for an animated page), \fI.ans\fR (ANSI) or \fI.txt\fR (plain text, shaded).
Image files are refused: prism-term writes text.
.TP
.BI banner " text ..."
Big text into scrollback (\fB\-\-font\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR, \fB\-\-palette\fR, \fB\-\-shadow\fR).
.TP
.BI "spin \-\- " "command ..."
Run a command under a spinner on stderr. Its stdout is passed through (streamed
to a pipe, or printed under the finished spinner on a terminal; \fB\-\-no\-passthrough\fR
swallows it); on failure its output is shown. Several words are an argv and reach
the program verbatim (on Windows nothing in them is expanded by cmd.exe, \fI%VAR%\fR
included); one quoted word is a shell command line. Exits with the command's status.
.TP
.B spinners
Preview every spinner.
.TP
.B dashboard
A live metrics dashboard demo (needs 100x34).
.TP
.B demo
A tour of the inline helpers.
.TP
.B caps
Detected capabilities and glyph test patterns (\fB\-\-json\fR).
.TP
.B themes
The Prism themes.
.TP
.B palettes
The gradient palettes.
.TP
.BI theme " [format]"
Prism Night or Day (\fB\-\-day\fR) as a color scheme for a terminal emulator,
to stdout or \fB\-o\fR \fIfile\fR: windows-terminal, iterm2, alacritty, kitty,
wezterm, ghostty, foot, gnome-terminal, konsole, xresources, vscode, ptyxis,
terminal-app, xfce4-terminal, and osc (one printf of OSC 4/10/11 codes that
recolors any xterm-compatible terminal for the session, also over SSH).
Nothing is installed and no configuration is touched.
.TP
.B help
Usage. \fB\-v\fR prints the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " id"
prism-dark (Prism Night), prism-light (Prism Day), a family such as primer, or auto.
.TP
.B \-\-day\fR, \fB\-\-night
The Day or Night member of the theme's family.
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " m"
braille | sextant | quad | half | ascii | auto (banner also: block).
.TP
.BI \-\-palette " name"
A gradient palette (prism, fire, ocean, aurora, ...; see \fBpalettes\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " key=value"
A facet parameter (repeatable), e.g. \fB\-\-set speed=2\fR. Unknown keys are refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " n"
Target frame rate, 1 to 240 (default 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " s"
Seconds per facet in playlists and the showcase.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
A fixed size in cells, up to 1000x500.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " n"
A deterministic seed.
.TP
.BI \-\-at " s"
The time of a snapshot (0 to 600 s); \fB\-\-frames\fR \fIn\fR (1 to 3600) for animated HTML.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " d"
Force the color depth: truecolor | 256 | 16 | mono.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
No Unicode at all. \fB\-\-sextant\fR / \fB\-\-no\-sextant\fR force sextant glyphs.
.TP
.B \-\-transparent
Keep the terminal's own background. Body text uses the terminal's own foreground,
and on an interactive terminal the background is asked for (OSC 11) to pick Day or Night.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hud
Hide the player's status bar.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-intro
Skip First Light, the catalog browser's opening beam.
.TP
.B \-\-reduced\-motion
No intro, wipes or sweeps.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output (list, galleries, info, caps). \fB\-\-ids\fR prints bare ids
(list, galleries, themes, palettes, theme) for shell completion.
.SH KEYS
In the catalog browser: arrows or hjkl move, Tab changes pane, Enter plays,
s showcase, / search, g gallery, f kind, t theme, d day/night, m mode, ? help, q quit.
In the live player: left/right facet, space pause, m mode, t theme, d day/night,
r restart, h HUD, q back. Ctrl-Z suspends both (fg resumes them); Ctrl-C quits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Mono output: pictures are drawn as a luminance ramp instead of color.
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
0 | 1 | 2 | 3: mono, 16, 256 or truecolor.
.TP
.B PRISM_TERM_DEPTH\fR, \fBPRISM_TERM_UNICODE\fR, \fBPRISM_TERM_SEXTANT
Override detection.
.TP
.B PRISM_TERM_THEME
A theme id, or day | night | auto.
.TP
.B LC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_CTYPE\fR, \fBLANG
The first one set decides Unicode (LC_ALL=C means 7-bit ASCII).
.TP
.B PRISM_REDUCED_MOTION\fR, \fBPRISM_TERM_INTRO
Reduced motion; PRISM_TERM_INTRO=0 skips the intro.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a runtime failure; 2 on a usage error (an unknown command,
option or value). \fBspin\fR exits with its command's status. A signal ends the
program with 128 plus its number: 130 for SIGINT (Ctrl-C), 129 for SIGHUP, 143 for SIGTERM.
.SH NOTES
Git Bash's mintty (without ConPTY) gives programs pipes instead of a console;
run \fBwinpty prism-term\fR there, or use Windows Terminal.
.PP
Without installing: \fBnpx \-y \-\-package=https://prism.jeremyfhall.com/dl/prism-term-0.2.0.tgz prism-term\fR
(checksums: https://prism.jeremyfhall.com/dl/SHA256SUMS; /dl/prism-term.tgz is the
latest-release alias). Browse with curl: \fBcurl \-sL prism.jeremyfhall.com/tty\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://prism.jeremyfhall.com/terminal/
